  "recommendation": "Select and SHA-256 verify these exact members from the already catalog-pinned initramfs. Package uncompressed .ko bytes and explicitly insmod the listed dependency order; no depmod, modprobe database, gzip support or new modloop input is needed for this fixed closure. Fail a guest stage if insmod, expected PCI/device enumeration or link/block setup fails. Modules alone do not establish transport correctness.",
  "limits": [
    "Raw block checks still need explicit bounded host-backed PCI block device and restart/persistence verification",
    "Filesystem checks need a separately pinned disk filesystem image and optional ext4 module closure",
    "Network checks need an explicit PCI network device, controlled reachable endpoint, byte-count/checksum validation and host evidence",
    "PCI, virtio core/ring and modern/legacy PCI transport are built in; do not add nonexistent virtio_pci.ko or virtio_ring.ko payloads",
    "The driver module bytes are uncompressed despite CONFIG_MODULE_COMPRESS_GZIP=y; preserve exact bytes without recompression",
    "AF_INET/AF_INET6 sockets use built-in kernel support; packet-socket tools would additionally need af_packet.ko because CONFIG_PACKET=m"
  ],
